Date: 7 Jan 88 01:25
From:	DSSDEV::HALLGRIMSSON "Eirikur, CDA Product Manager
Subject: some feedback on new MAC Kermit, f.y.i.
Keywords: MacKermit 0.9(36)b4

This is a fine update of the original Mac Kermit. I was able to remap my
separate keypad easily, but I had to know the characters to transmit for
each key. It's a good VT100 emulator. Runs Emacs, EVE, Notes, etc., just
fine.

It seems to be hardwired for the modem port--there's no selection that I
could find.  Oh, well, it's preliminary...

The VAX Kermit that I have on DSSDEV has a transmit packet maximum of 90,
making the turnaround time annoying.

This new Kermit works really well under MultiFinder. I put up MultiFinder
just for this, (don't have it on my hard disk yet) and I could have a file
transfer going, be editing in MS-Word, and use the Finder all at once.

