Date: Mon, 04 Jan 88 13:35:07 -0500
From: abe@j.cc.purdue.edu (Vic Abell)
Subject: MacKermit 0.9(36)b4
Keywords: MacKermit 0.9(36)

It's really a pleasure to have a long packet MacKermit at last.  Several
rough edges persist, however:

1. Cloverleaf-R doesn't isn't the equivalent of selecting
   "Receive File" from the menu.

2. If the receive packet size is set to 1024, MacKermit and
   Kermit enter a retry loop.  (Sizes up to 1000 seem to work
   properly.)  Clicking on Cancel calls up an "OK" dialog box
   whose text is the first part of the file being transferred.
   Perhaps the receive buffer is too short.

3. I have been unable to set the send packet size to anything
   other than 90 and have the setting remain.

