Date: Tue, 29 Dec 87 17:45:35 EST
From: Chris Schanzle <chris@umbc3.UMD.EDU>
Subject: Macintosh Kermit wants/wishes before 1.0 release
Keywords: MacKermit

There are two things I feel must be included in Kermit before the 1.0
release.  First is an EDIT menu!  Why can't one select text with the mouse,
cut and paste with the clipboard?  ALL Macintosh terminal programs should be
able to do this.

The second one here could be an oversight on my part, but how does/can one
change the volume to receive files?  Moving my default document around to
different download disks is a pain.  (if you double-click on the settings
document that resides on another volume, that volume will be come the
default receive volume.)  Others have implemented it by putting up a
"SFgetvol" box, showing the amount of space available on each volume.  I
would prefer a dialog box showing all mounted (and unmounted) volumes
displaying lots of neat info, allowing you to simply select a volume by
clicking on it, it then being highlighted, then press <RETURN> or the <OK>
box.

One final bit if strangeness: Kermit .9(36)b3 responds to the inquery
terminal with "<ESC>[?1;2c".  This is how the old VersaTerm responds, and a
termcap entry for our unix machine allows insert/delete character in the
middle of the line (thereby not having to redraw the rest of the line, a
real timesaver at 1200 baud!).  Kermit deletes characters out of the middle
of the line properly, but inserts are "typeovers", that is, it doesn't shove
the end of the line to the right.

Kermit sure has come a long way in the last year or two!  Thanks guys!

			- Chris Schanzle
ARPA   : chris@umbc3.UMD.EDU		BITNET : chris@umbc
"He was betrayed by the limits of his own potential."

------------------------------

Date: Wed, 30 Dec 87 15:08:10 CST
From: brian@sally.utexas.edu (Brian H. Powell)
Subject: Impressions of MacKermit 0.9(36)b4
Keywords: MacKermit 0.9(36)

     This version of kermit seems to be an improvement over 0.9(36)b2, but
it's still got some problems:

	* I set option to mean meta.  This yields apparent nonsense.  e.g.,

		option-		should be	yields
		  A		\301		\201
		  a		\341		\214
		  b		\342		\272
		  c		\343		\215
		  d		\344		\266
			etc. etc.

	* There still seems to be a problem with dead keys.  For example, you
	  have to press option-e twice before it sends anything.

	* The bug concerning improper updating of the screen after dialog
	  boxes are removed persists.  (i.e., sometimes 1) a dialog box is
	  removed, 2) the screen is updated, 3) the area under the dialog box
	  is erased (filled with white).)

	* An unrelated bug in the update procedure:  items in reverse video
	  are not updated properly.  For example, if you are running emacs,
	  the mode line is typically in reverse video.  If you bring up the
	  "response" window, for example, the mode line is updated in
	  non-reverse mode (i.e., black on white).

	* Cmd-key equivalents still appear in the menu, even if you've turned
	  them off.

Besides fixing these things, I'd also like to see the following:
	* Because the new MacKermit uses the new serial driver, it hangs up
	  the phone when the program quits.  (i.e., it drops DTR.)  I'd like
	  to see it issue the _Control call to not negate DTR when the program
	  quits.  (See csCode=16 on page IV-226 (The Serial Driver) in Inside
	  Mac Volume IV.)

     Thanks for fixing the other bugs.  I'm nearly confident enough to replace
my use of 0.8(34) with this version.

Brian H. Powell
		UUCP:	...!uunet!ut-sally!brian
		ARPA:	brian@sally.UTEXAS.EDU

		P.O. Box 5899
		Austin, TX 78763-5899
		(512) 346-0835

