Date: 3 Feb 88 09:08
To: f_dacruz%aqua.DEC@decwrl.dec.com
Subject: MAC KERMIT (2 of 2), "secure VMS KERMIT"

Frank,

	Here's some more comments on the new MAC KERMIT.

	Also, I read a note about someone requesting a "secure" VMS KERMIT.
	The "problem" with spawning subprocess can be prevent by modifying
	the system authorization file (sort of like /etc/passwd) to not
	allow subprocesses for that user.  Of course, that affects ALL
	attempts by that user to use such... not just in KERMIT.  I would
	also suggest that they "solve" the file-protection problem by
	using the normal VMS UIC-based and new ACL-based protection schemes.

						--Dan S.

